Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:06.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,There was a little café where Rahel and\NBekele met every Friday.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.04,0:00:10.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Rahel knew just how Bekele liked his\Ncoffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.85,0:00:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,When Rahel didn’t smile, Bekele knew a\Nhard day lay behind it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.09,0:00:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,But she never knew that he loved her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.72,0:00:27.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,One afternoon, Rahel told him she’d\Nfound a job in another city.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.40,0:00:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and said, “My hero, you\Nknow how proud I am of you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.18,0:00:40.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,That night, Bekele typed, “There was\Nsomething I wanted to tell you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.80,0:00:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then his thumb stopped over send.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.89,0:00:47.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,But he deleted the message.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.32,0:00:53.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was afraid that the truth coming out\Nmight change their friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.56,0:00:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they reached the bus station, Rahel\Nsaid she was scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.87,0:01:03.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele carried her bag and walked with\Nher.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.52,0:01:08.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before she boarded the bus, she packed\Nhim a little coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.77,0:01:12.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,“So we don’t miss our Friday coffee,”\Nshe said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.06,0:01:19.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as the bus pulled away, his phone\Nlit up: “Friday. Same as always?”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.89,0:01:24.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and typed, “I’ll be\Nthere.”
